  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Biology A.S. Degree - Cal-GETC GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published September 04, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7715/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Official Total Units: 60-63; this seed models the first-listed/recommended General Biology & Pre-Med path = 14 + 14 + 17 + 15 = 60 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page; Area 2 math at 3 units, the low path). Semester sums verified against the map's 14-15 / 14-16 / 17 / 15 headers. Distinct from the Biology AS (Local GE) (map 7631). PATH SELECTION (documented): the map offers two paths — General Biology & Pre-Med (BIOL 402, 412, 422; CHEM 400) and Allied Health (CHEM 305/309/400; BIOL 430, 431, 440). The printed semester units only work with the General Biology & Pre-Med path: the Sem 4 List B slot is 5 units, and the Allied Health recommendation (BIOL 440, 4 units) does not fill it, while BIOL 422 (5 units) does. Modeled: Sem 1 CHEM 400 (Gen Bio path; Allied Health allows CHEM 305/309/400); Sem 2 List A BIOL 402; Sem 3 List A BIOL 412 + List B BIOL 302; Sem 4 List B BIOL 422. List A minimum 10 units satisfied (BIOL 402 + BIOL 412 = 10). List B minimum 8 units satisfied (BIOL 302 + BIOL 422 = 8). Choice slots: (1) GE ENGL C1000 / * H+ 488 / + ESLW 340, Area 1A — ENGL C1000 selected; (2) ME CHEM 305 / 309 / 400 Introduction to Chemistry (5), Areas 5A/5C — CHEM 400 selected (Gen Bio path); (3) Elec INDIS 313 / HCD 310 — INDIS 313 selected; (4) GE Mathematical Concepts & Quantitative Reasoning, Area 2 (3-5) — generic 3-unit slot (choose per STEM placement); (5) List A slots — BIOL 402 / BIOL 412 selected; (6) List B 3-unit slot — BIOL 302 selected (first-listed 3-unit List B course); (7) List B 5-unit slot — BIOL 422 selected. Documented prerequisites: CHEM 400 requires CHEM 300 (C or better within one year) or ACS placement exam AND Intermediate Algebra; BIOL 402 requires CHEM 400; BIOL 412/422 require BIOL 402; BIOL 430 requires CHEM 305/309/400; BIOL 431 requires BIOL 430; BIOL 434 requires BIOL 431; BIOL 440 requires CHEM 305/309/400; BIOL 362 requires BIOL 305; BIOL C1001L coreq BIOL C1001; BIOL 315 coreq BIOL 314; BIOL 327 coreq BIOL 326. Students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo. Area 4 rule: the Sem 4 Area 4 course must be in a different discipline than the Sem 3 Area 4 course. AA/AS requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, Cal-GETC Areas 1-6 with 'C' or better. Electives: any courses numbered 100-499. Biology, Science, Math, & Engineering Meta Majors. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
